  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. A page of weights/KV cache that doesn't fit in GPU HBM lives in Grace's LPDDR5X. Because NVLink-C2C is cache-coherent, this CPU memory acts as an extension of GPU memory — just slower (384 GB/s vs 8 TB/s).",
      "focus": ["lpddr5x-left", "lpddr5x-right"],
      "dot": "lpddr5x-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": "grace-detail",
      "stage": "cpu-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Inside the Grace die, the 72 Neoverse V2 cores and the SCF mesh resolve the request; the 114 MB L3 may already hold the page from a previous access.",
      "focus": ["core-grid", "scf-fabric", "l3-slice"],
      "dot": "scf-fabric",
      "drill": "grace-detail",
      "stage": "scf-mesh"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. NVLink-C2C carries the page to the GPU at up to 900 GB/s with full hardware cache coherency — no explicit memcpy in the application code.",
      "focus": ["c2c-link-gpu0"],
      "dot": "c2c-link-gpu0",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "c2c"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. The migrated data lands in an HBM3e stack on B300 #0 (288 GB per GPU at 8 TB/s, in 12-Hi stacks).",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-left-gpu0", "hbm-base-left-gpu0"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-left-gpu0",
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. The memory controller attached to die 0 reads the HBM3e stack next to it.",
      "focus": ["mc-die0-gpu0"],
      "dot": "mc-die0-gpu0",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. If the tile actually lives behind die 1, it crosses NV-HBI between the two Blackwell Ultra dies at 10 TB/s — invisible to software, same mechanism as on B200.",
      "focus": ["nv-hbi-gpu0"],
      "dot": "nv-hbi-gpu0",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Data settles in the shared L2 cache of die 0.",
      "focus": ["l2-die0-gpu0"],
      "dot": "l2-die0-gpu0",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. TMA copies A and B tiles from L2 into an SM's shared memory, asynchronously.",
      "focus": ["tma"],
      "dot": "tma",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tma"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Tiles sit in shared memory, ready for the Tensor Cores.",
      "focus": ["smem"],
      "dot": "smem",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. One thread issues tcgen05.mma: the 4 fifth-gen Tensor Cores multiply the tiles, e.g. in NVFP4.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "11. Partial sums accumulate in TMEM (not registers) across K; once done, CUDA cores run the epilogue — bias, activation, quantize.",
      "focus": ["tmem", "register-file"],
      "dot": "tmem",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "12. Results go back to HBM; tensor-parallel results all-reduce over NVLink 5 (1.8 TB/s) to GPU #1 / the NVL72 rack, or back over NVLink-C2C to Grace for CPU-side post-processing.",
      "focus": ["nvlink-die0-gpu0", "c2c-link-gpu0"],
      "dot": "nvlink-die0-gpu0",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
